{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794176517,"nonce":"vQsAWnjeuWADoYrWoLCSe8FrLz0=","title":"schema and schema export hide archived entries unless --include-archive","message":"A follow-up to 4317136, which made the schema print archived types, fields and values marked `archived: true`, so that export followed by import changes nothing. On this repository that brings back the six preset types pruned in October: 65 archived entries, in 759 lines.\n\nHiding them loses nothing, because an import leaves what a file omits as it stands, and `--prune` skips what is already archived.\n\n## Design (approved by the user)\n\n- `git work schema` and `git work schema export` leave out archived types, fields and values by default. `--include-archive` puts them back, marked `archived: true`, matching `issue list`. Starlark takes `include_archive=True`, on the same host path.\n- `export | import` remains a no-op either way.\n- The jira sync's derive and dry run, and anything else reading the export internally, still see archived entries where they need them: derive must unarchive what Jira lists again.\n- The design documents, the quickstart and the generated docs change in the same change.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["issue-model","cli"],"parent":"8ade81134de7c2f5d1a16c3a48efc761b35bbf4cc2a58eaf8189fa5c15621e01","priority":"medium","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}